1                          ; SMP-S2: internal (E12) sample playback with a lo-fi
 splice time-stretch.
2                          ; The engine is shared with SMP-ST (rom_stretch); see
 stretch_engine.inc.
3         000000           BANK_ID   equ     0                                 ;
 SAMPLE_INFO / SAMPLE_READ bank: INTERNAL
4                                    include 'stretch_engine.inc'
5                          ; Shared engine of SMP-ST (UW ROM) and SMP-T2 (intern
al E12 samples): sample
6                          ; playback with a lo-fi splice time-stretch (S950 sty
le). The wrapper defines
7                          ; BANK_ID, the SAMPLE_INFO / SAMPLE_READ bank: 0 inte
rnal, 1 UW ROM, or -1 for
8                          ; both: SMPL 0..UW_SLOTS-1 are UW ROM slots, the sett
ings after them internal
9                          ; slots (the wrapper then also defines UW_SLOTS).
10                         ;
11                         ; One grain plays at a time. A playhead moves through
 the sample, slowed by TIME.
12                         ; Every GRAN output samples, on a 32-sample block bou
ndary, a new grain starts
13                         ; near the playhead, centred on it and offset by a ra
ndom FLUX amount, and the
14                         ; two grains crossfade over the next 4 blocks (128 sa
mples). The splice is
15                         ; worked out at the end of an ordinary block, and PTC
H and TIME are re-read
16                         ; only outside crossfades, which keeps the crossfade 
blocks (two sample reads)
17                         ; inside the cycle budget. PTCH sets the grain read r
ate, so time and pitch are
18                         ; independent. Grains read straight on past the windo
w (no wrapping); a grain
19                         ; about to run out of the window splices back to the 
playhead early. The voice
20                         ; fades out over 4 blocks when the playhead reaches E
ND; TIME 127 freezes it.
21                         ; DEC decays the level; 127 holds it.
22                         ;
23                         ; END before STRT plays the sample in reverse, from S
TRT back to END. The
24                         ; engine always runs forwards through the window lo..
hi; in reverse, POSGEN
25                         ; reads at floor(lo + hi - 1 - p) instead of floor(p)
.
26                         ;
27                         ; Parameters, Y:(r6+1..8):
28                         ;   1 PTCH  raw14 bipolar  (setting - 64) / 2 semiton
es: -32..+32, 1/256 steps between
29                         ;   2 SMPL  index          slot in the bank: UW 0..47
, internal 0..20 (latched at TRIG)
30                         ;   3 DEC   raw14          decay, 60 dB in 0.03..30 s
; 127 = no decay
31                         ;   4 TIME  raw14          playhead slow-down from a 
table: 0 normal, 42 half, 127 frozen
32                         ;   5 STRT  unipolar Q23   start as a fraction of the
 sample; 127 = its end (latched)
33                         ;   6 END   unipolar Q23   end as a fraction; 127 = w
hole sample (latched)
34                         ;   7 GRAN  squared Q23    grain length 300 + 4776*s 
output samples (300..5000)
Motorola DSP56300 Assembler  Version 6.3.15   26-10-11  01:36:47  
stretch_engine.inc  Page 2



35                         ;   8 FLUX  unipolar Q23   jitter: position up to +-0
.75 grain, length +-37.5%
36                         ;
37                         ; Persistent Y state (Y+9: the latched bank when BANK
_ID is -1, otherwise unused):
38                         ;  10 active  11/12 grain position int/frac  13/14 pl
ayhead int/frac
39                         ;  15 lo  16 hi  17 hi-lo  18 native step (Q16.16)  1
9 samples to next splice
40                         ;  20 gain reached at the end of the last block  21 r
andom seed  22 slot
41                         ;  23 reverse  24 lo + hi - 1  25 decay envelope  26 
end fade step (0 = none, 1..4)
42                         ;  27 crossfade step (0 = none, 1..4)  28/29 old grai
n position int/frac
43                         ; Rates, recomputed in every block outside a crossfad
e:
44                         ;  30/31 grain rate (24.24)  32 grain rate * 2^17  49
/50 twice the grain rate
45                         ;  35/36 playhead step per block (24.24)  37 playhead
 rate * 2^17
46                         ; Y scratch within one RENDER (services clobber most 
registers):
47                         ;  33 PTCH fraction  34 octave + 6  38/39 gain at blo
ck start/end
48                         ;  40/41 old grain gain start/step  42/43 new grain g
ain start/step
49                         ;  44 K  45 GRAN  46 64 * GRAN  47 J  48 centring
